  "name": "Transition through three times of a schedule",
  "description": "A 100 MVA generator and a load at a 110 kV bus, 30 km from a grid of 5000 MVA, followed through three hours of a schedule in one run (made by openkeito.pandapower.transition(net, plan, times=\"all\", start_time_s=0.5, ramp_time_s=1, settle_time_s=6, load_steps=2)). Load: 70 MW and 20 Mvar, then 90 and 25, then 60 and 15. Generator: 60 MW, then 75, then 55, at 1.02 pu; the grid delivers the rest. The run starts from the power flow of the first hour. From 0.5 s the set points move over 1 s to those of the second hour, and the run settles for 6 s; from 7.5 s they move to those of the third hour, and it settles until 14.5 s. The hours between are not run. The generator has an excitation system (gen0_efd), a governor (gen0_valve, gen0_pm) and a stabilizer (gen0_pss) made of control blocks; gen0_dpref and gen0_dvref are the changes of its load and voltage references that the power flows of the three hours ask for. The load is the impedance of each hour: load0 is what all three hours have, load0_out* what the third no longer has and load0_in* what only the second has, each in two parts behind switches that act at a quarter and at three quarters of the ramp. The grid is a source whose internal voltage (ext_grid0_ed, ext_grid0_eq) moves with the power flows. At 7.5 s and at 14.5 s the bus voltages are within 1e-4 pu, and the power of the generator within 0.01 MW, of the power flow of the second and of the third hour.",
